============================================================================
A. UNDRIVEN + DISSIPATIVE -- what both documents actually specify
============================================================================
  Q(0) = 7.2736   ->   Q(tau=60) = 2.955e-04      monotone decay
  max Re eig(-i Hbar - Gam/2) = -0.0710
  => single global attractor at z=0. 'Equilibrium maintained' is FALSE here.

============================================================================
B. DRIVEN-DISSIPATIVE    dz/dtau = -i Hbar z - (1/2) Gam z + D
============================================================================
  exact NESS: ||dz/dtau|| = 1.11e-15
  n_C = 9.062256    n_S = 9.030100    Q = 18.092355

  PER-SUBSTRATE BALANCE AT NESS  (each must vanish)
    dn_C/dtau = -J - sig_C + P_C = +2.665e-15
    dn_S/dtau = +J - sig_S + P_S = -8.882e-16
      J (carbon->silicon flux) = +0.451505
      sig_C = gam_C n_C = 2.718677     sig_S = gam_S n_S = 0.451505
      P_C = 2Re<a,D_C> = +3.170182     P_S = 2Re<b,D_S> = +0.000000

  POWER-BALANCE THEOREM (the open-system replacement for dQ/dtau=0)
    Re(z^dag D) = (1/2)(sig_C + sig_S)
      LHS = 1.5850908209     RHS = 1.5850908209     residual 6.66e-16
    Proof: Hbar Hermitian => z^dag Hbar z real => Re(z^dag(-i Hbar)z)=0;
           Re(z^dag D) - (1/2) z^dag Gam z = 0 at NESS.

  G IS LOAD-BEARING: carbon drive alone sustains silicon occupation
    with G : n_S = 9.030100
    with G=0: n_S = 0.000e+00   <- silicon starves exactly

  TRANSDUCTION EFFICIENCY  n_S / Re(z^dag D) = 5.6969  [nats per unit drive power]
  note n_S/n_C = 0.9965 -- near equipartition because gam_S << gam_C:
       the weakly-damped substrate accumulates charge until its sink matches the flux.
